omx-plugins (0.10.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.10.0: plugins described in omx-contract's words, faces checked
    against them; omx-contract 2.15.0 and omx-dsp 0.22.0
  * debian: with no omx-contract command, skip the generator checks and say so
  * eq-identity, the EQ default probe: the EQ's names are omx-dsp's
  * descriptor-view: from omx-contract 2.15.0 on, a schema not found is red
  * omx-contract: a union render carries its owners beside it
  * packaging: build with the omx-contract command, the package that installs
    it
  * omx-contract: read a 2.15 contract directory through the CLI's union
    render
  * face-descriptor: our built faces, scanned, against the authored descriptor
  * descriptor-view: each descriptor holds to omx-contract's descriptor words
  * plugins: every single-kernel plugin described in omx-contract's words
  * omx-delay: described in omx-contract's words, its declaration the extras
  * gen: a plugin's declaration may be the view of its descriptor
  * docs: the declaration as a view of the plugin descriptor
  * omx-transient: generated faces follow its family none
  * omx-transient: no dynamics family; a declared family stands on its
    meanings (#138)
  * panel-description: lay a panel out from a plugin descriptor of any origin
    (#145)
  * docs: a panel laid out from a plugin descriptor, its widget step and its
    family from meanings
  * private-refs-check: self-test arms only the dated-filename and
    dated-citation patterns can catch
  * Refuse AI-attribution lines in commit messages: commit-msg hook and a
    pull request check
  * qualify-release: read plugin-qualify.rt-safety/1 and /2, refuse an
    unknown schema
  * ci: the package jobs hand static-table-host the test plugins' ids (#162)
  * omx-test-note-echo: a test instrument, one note out per note in (#162)
  * omx-test-transport-probe: a test probe that records each block's
    transport (#162)
  * omx-test-sine-voice: a test instrument, one sine per held note (#162)
  * Test plugins: a declaration's "role": "test" links a face and installs
    nothing (#162)
  * tools: the declaration schema's validator in a module of its own (#162)

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:01:50 +0000
